  "ref": "2KI.17.18",
  "review_notes": [
    "The flagged three-morpheme unit לְבַדּוֹ → *only* is not indivisible as it stood. Rule 30's own sentence on compound prepositions holds that a pronominal suffix on the construct noun is no part of the fusion in either direction: it takes whatever pronoun the ASV writes for it, or goes unrepresented where none is written. *only* carries the preposition's relation and בַּד's lexeme but nothing of the 3ms suffix, and rule 30 forbids absorbing a morpheme whose sense the rendering does not carry.",
    "This matches the chapter's own treatment of the same shape at 2KI.17.34, where שָׂם שְׁמוֹ → *named* fuses the verb and the noun and leaves the suffix unrepresented."
  ]
